{
 "duration": 77.087,
 "method": "ffmpeg silencedetect -35dB 0.25s; phrases mapped in script order",
 "segments": [
  {
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 1.688,
   "text": "Here's a strange experiment."
  },
  {
   "start": 2.165,
   "end": 7.436,
   "text": "Students at MIT were asked to write down the last two digits of their social security number."
  },
  {
   "start": 7.851,
   "end": 8.859,
   "text": "Just a random number."
  },
  {
   "start": 9.71,
   "end": 11.256,
   "text": "Then they bid on things."
  },
  {
   "start": 11.659,
   "end": 12.272,
   "text": "A keyboard."
  },
  {
   "start": 12.606,
   "end": 13.046,
   "text": "Wine."
  },
  {
   "start": 13.359,
   "end": 13.829,
   "text": "Chocolate."
  },
  {
   "start": 14.429,
   "end": 17.708,
   "text": "And that random number changed what they were willing to pay."
  },
  {
   "start": 18.325,
   "end": 22.503,
   "text": "The students with the highest numbers offered about fifty-six dollars for the keyboard."
  },
  {
   "start": 23.028,
   "end": 24.21,
   "text": "The students with the lowest?"
  },
  {
   "start": 24.607,
   "end": 25.593,
   "text": "About sixteen."
  },
  {
   "start": 26.19,
   "end": 27.501,
   "text": "For the same keyboard."
  },
  {
   "start": 28.158,
   "end": 30.048,
   "text": "Psychologists call it anchoring."
  },
  {
   "start": 30.497,
   "end": 32.972,
   "text": "The first number you see becomes a starting point,"
  },
  {
   "start": 33.285,
   "end": 36.151,
   "text": "and every judgment after it is adjusted from there."
  },
  {
   "start": 36.685,
   "end": 37.935,
   "text": "Usually not enough."
  },
  {
   "start": 38.534,
   "end": 39.965,
   "text": "Now think about a store."
  },
  {
   "start": 40.374,
   "end": 42.898,
   "text": "A three-hundred-dollar jacket hangs by the door."
  },
  {
   "start": 43.398,
   "end": 46.474,
   "text": "The hundred-and-twenty-dollar one beside it"
  },
  {
   "start": 46.751,
   "end": 47.319,
   "text": "suddenly feels..."
  },
  {
   "start": 47.895,
   "end": 48.635,
   "text": "reasonable."
  },
  {
   "start": 48.934,
   "end": 51.041,
   "text": "A tag says \"was two hundred, now one-twenty.\""
  },
  {
   "start": 51.614,
   "end": 54.411,
   "text": "That crossed-out price isn't information."
  },
  {
   "start": 54.832,
   "end": 55.682,
   "text": "It's an anchor."
  },
  {
   "start": 56.247,
   "end": 57.786,
   "text": "And here's the unsettling part."
  },
  {
   "start": 58.237,
   "end": 59.237,
   "text": "In that experiment,"
  },
  {
   "start": 59.508,
   "end": 61.407,
   "text": "the anchor was completely random."
  },
  {
   "start": 61.807,
   "end": 62.596,
   "text": "It meant nothing."
  },
  {
   "start": 63.232,
   "end": 64.346,
   "text": "It still worked."
  },
  {
   "start": 64.955,
   "end": 67.786,
   "text": "So next time the first number you see feels fair,"
  },
  {
   "start": 68.117,
   "end": 69.276,
   "text": "ask one question:"
  },
  {
   "start": 69.841,
   "end": 71.3,
   "text": "where did that number come from?"
  },
  {
   "start": 71.872,
   "end": 74.367,
   "text": "Because the first number isn't always the right one."
  },
  {
   "start": 74.834,
   "end": 77.087,
   "text": "It's just the one that got there first."
  }
 ]
}